    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπί-φορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inclined, prone</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τι</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				990
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.43
			</span></i> O.; esp. of authors who are fond of particular phrases,
			freq. in Gramm., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί</span> . . Sch.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				693
			</span></i>: c. inf., Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρως</span>
			v.l. in Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.207
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἔχειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					1.2.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>leading easily</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸς ἐπί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					10.46
				</span></i>
			.</div>
